{:answer/id #uuid "b9613734-b36b-570c-b742-01de24e71c7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{4s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346588} {:answer/id #uuid "3b62673a-4f0f-58db-a33a-99e632bab64d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346589} {:answer/id #uuid "900b4351-1866-5168-8219-f1bae36d1c1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{4s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346590} {:answer/id #uuid "12ca04c1-e43f-5fd4-a5f0-6eb2e1f1eb13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "900b4351-1866-5168-8219-f1bae36d1c1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{4s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346590} :answer-field/id #uuid "788c11de-3913-5a8c-92f0-f0bd7942afd5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346587} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8701655a-28e3-54ab-82b8-b58886091404" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346593} {:answer/id #uuid "e804a845-d631-56c5-9306-ee85e325ea58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346594} {:answer/id #uuid "6ae4c6de-bbdd-5180-b019-0eb9f36127b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346595} {:answer/id #uuid "4e909d91-5565-52de-be9f-5b2ae0c6ce92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346596} {:answer/id #uuid "2d6eea4e-0a96-5bb5-a7d8-12ce6470c5a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge -\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8701655a-28e3-54ab-82b8-b58886091404" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346593} :answer-field/id #uuid "28795fda-d7e8-5233-a162-5591e3297c7f" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94367c71-7085-5306-a074-f64a7fe19734" :question/math-academy-id "q-340733" :question/problem "Complete the arguments in the reasoning below to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{-t/4}.$First, we apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=F(s)={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nWe now examine the convergence of $F(s)$ for different values of $s:$\n\n$\\,$ For {{field-2}}\nthe integral is divergent.\n\n$\\,$ For {{field-3}}\nthe integral is convergent.\n\nEvaluating our integral in the convergent case, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t={{field-4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $L{{e}^{-t/4}}=\\frac{4}{4s+1},$ \ndefined for\n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(t)$ defined on $[0,\\infty ),$ the Laplace transform of $f,$ denoted $L{f(t)}$ or $F(s),$ is a function of the variable $s$ defined as\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nprovided that this integral exists and is finite. \n\nFor the function $f(t)={e}^{-t/4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{-t/4}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st-t/4}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the last integral, we must consider whether $s\\ne -\\frac{1}{4}$ or $s=-\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\n- If $s\\ne -\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{-1/4-s}{e}^{(-1/4-s)t})|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1/4-s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}(1-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}-\\frac{1}{s+1/4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate the limit. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & s>-\\frac{1}{4}, \\\\ \\infty ,\\, & s<-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $s=-\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-\\frac{1}{4}) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(-1/4-(-1/4))t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{0t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }t\\,{|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(a-0) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }a \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- For $s\\le -\\frac{1}{4}$ the integral is divergent.\n\n- For $s>-\\frac{1}{4}$ the integral is convergent.\n\nEvaluating for $s>-\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}-\\frac{1}{s+1/4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}-\\frac{1}{s+1/4}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4s+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{-t/4}$ is $F(s)=\\frac{4}{4s+1},$ defined for $s>-\\frac{1}{4}.$"}]}
